  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "A major is a senior military officer (O-4) in the US Army, Air Force, or Marines ranking above captain and below lieutenant colonel. They earn roughly $7,000–$12,000+ monthly based on experience, acting as primary staff officers or company commanders. Academically, it is a student's specialized college field. Military Rank (Major, O-4) Role: Key staff officers for brigade-level planning or Executive Officers (XO) in battalions. Requirements: Requires a bachelor's degree, completion of officer candidate/training school, and several years of service as a commissioned officer. Salary: Dependent on pay grade (O-4) and years of service (Basic Pay + Allowances for Housing/Subsistence). Academic Major Definition: The primary subject area a college student chooses to specialize in, comprising one-third to one-half of their coursework. Types: Examples include arts/humanities (literature, art), business (finance, marketing), health/medicine, and sciences. Common Definitions Importance: Signifying something \"great,\" \"large,\" or \"significant\". Age: Referring to a person of legal age. Music: A scale or key with specific intervals.",
